    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d395-a1">

                <pb facs="0395" n="371" sameAs="frus:frus1864p4/pg371"/>

                <head>[Circular.]</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States of
                                America</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1863-08-06"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 6,
                        1863</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Information has been received at this
                    legation that a steamer, recently built in England, and called the Southerner,
                    is about to proceed to the Mediterranean, under the command of Captain Page, of
                    the rebel navy, for the purpose of preying on the commerce of the United
                    States.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to request that you will advise me by telegraph should said
                    vessel make her appearance in your vicinity; and that you will also telegraph
                    the same to the commander of the nearest United States vessel of war, or to any
                    consul through whom intelligence may be most promptly communicated to him. The
                    utmost vigilance is expected of you in this respect.</p>
                <p>Respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>E. JOY MORRIS.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
